<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse halts trade on Alphatec.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse halts trade on Alphatec.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand on Wednesday halted trading of Alphatec Electronics Plc's shares pending the outcome of its negotiations with creditor banks on the company's debt restructuring.</p>
<p>Alphatec has been in talks with creditor banks led by Bangkok Bank Plc on restructuring its financial profile after a recent pullout by Texas Instruments from two joint ventures with the Thai company.</p>
<p>Texas Instruments withdrew after their projects failed to receive bank financing.</p>
<p>Alphatec said earlier it had held talks with Motorola Inc on the possibility of taking it on as an alternative partner.</p>
<p>Alphatec closed Tuesday at 31.50 baht.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom</p>
</text>
